  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Resource Development / Acquire Access", "technique": "T1650", "what_happened": "At 2027-09-08 02:14:07 CEST, a single clean HTTP GET to /remote/login on the FortiVPN gateway 10.108.57.10 originated from data.srcip=185.220.101.34. There was NO preceding port scan, NO directory enumeration, NO login-page crawl from this IP — exactly one request. The attacker already knew the exact portal URL. This is the defining T1650 signal: the access vector (the URL plus, shortly after, valid credentials) was acquired out-of-band — purchased from an Initial Access Broker marketplace — rather than discovered through reconnaissance.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 31100 'Web request to VPN login portal' fired with data.srcip=185.220.101.34 and data.dstip=10.108.57.10. The univariate anomaly: an external public IP with ZERO prior history in the SIEM touching the VPN portal exactly once, with no recon footprint before it.", "first_seen": "2027-09-08T02:14:07+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Initial Access / Valid Accounts", "technique": "T1078", "what_happened": "At 02:17:55 CEST (~4 minutes after the liveness GET), a single POST to /remote/logincheck from the same data.srcip=185.220.101.34 authenticated SUCCESSFULLY as data.win.eventdata.targetUserName=contractor.smith (domain CORP). The corresponding Windows authentication event 4624 was logged on the VPN gateway with logonType 3 and data.win.eventdata.ipAddress=185.220.101.34. CRITICAL ANOMALY: there were ZERO failed authentication attempts (event 4625) from this IP — or for this account from any external IP — before the success. A legitimate first-time remote login is preceded by enrollment, MFA registration, or at minimum a fat-finger failed attempt. A brute-force or password-spray shows many 4625 before a 4624. This shows NEITHER: it is a clean first-attempt success from a never-before-seen external IP = pre-acquired valid credentials.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 5710 'Auth Success from Unknown External IP — Zero Prior Failures' fired, correlating Windows event 4624 (data.win.eventdata.targetUserName=contractor.smith, data.win.eventdata.ipAddress=185.220.101.34, logonType 3) with the ABSENCE of any 4625 for the same account/IP in the preceding 30 days. rule.mitre.id T1078 (Valid Accounts) attached automatically.", "first_seen": "2027-09-08T02:17:55+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Initial Access / Threat-Intel Correlation", "technique": "T1078", "what_happened": "The successful VPN session at 02:17:55 originated from data.srcip=185.220.101.34, an IP that Wazuh's threat-intel integration flagged as a known Tor exit node / bulletproof VPS. Rule 5715 'VPN Login from Threat-Intel Listed IP' fired immediately on the same session. No contractor, employee, or vendor legitimately connects to the corporate VPN through a Tor exit node — this single fact alone elevates the session from anomalous to hostile.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 5715 fired when data.srcip=185.220.101.34 from the event 4624 VPN session matched the threat-intel blocklist feed. The combination of rule 5710 (zero-prior-failure success) AND rule 5715 (TI-listed source) on the SAME session is the canonical acquired-access fingerprint.", "first_seen": "2027-09-08T02:17:58+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Discovery / Account + Endpoint Discovery", "technique": "T1087", "what_happened": "Within 90 seconds of the VPN session establishing (02:19:33 onward), the contractor.smith session made a rapid burst of accesses: the internal admin portal on 10.108.57.40 (/portal/admin/dashboard, /portal/admin/users), internal file repositories (/portal/files/finance, /portal/files/hr), and API user-enumeration endpoints (/api/v1/users?admin=true, /api/v1/roles). No legitimate contractor session begins with admin-dashboard and HR-file access within 90 seconds of first login. This immediate, aggressive, high-value-target enumeration is the behavior of an attacker assessing the worth of freshly-acquired access — not an employee doing their job.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 5501 'Multiple Internal Endpoint Access Within 60s of Login' and rule 31501 'User Enumeration via API Post-Auth' fired, correlating the event 4624 session (data.win.eventdata.targetUserName=contractor.smith) with a burst of web-access alerts to data.dstip=10.108.57.40 admin/file/API paths in the 02:19:33-02:27:10 window. rule.mitre.id T1087 (Account Discovery) attached.", "first_seen": "2027-09-08T02:19:33+0200"}
  ],
